Z||000007||Tweek||06-24-2001||07:29 AM||||One thing with AUS's though, since his was in km/h and 180 at that, as opposed to 140 I think. (like how you can have 85 mph and 120 mph) I did a little math and figured that for about every 11 of his mrks, it equaled about 10 mph, so I had to go in and adjust the bold marks and long ones like so...   and I also used the same template for the tach, only it was like 14.5 marks to every 1000 rpms..  lol<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierofrek||06-24-2001||07:50 AM||||yep, the numbers I came up with are:<BR>MPH     KM/H<BR>5---        8.04<BR>10---       16.09<BR>15---       24.14<BR>20---       32.18<BR>25---       40.23<BR>30---       48.28<BR>35---       56.32<BR>40---       64.37<BR>45---       72.42<BR>50---       80.00<BR>55---       88.51<BR>60---       96.56<BR>65---       104.60<BR>70---       112.65<BR>75---       120.70<BR>80---       128.74<BR>85---       136.79<p>[This message has been edited by fierofrek (edited 06-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tweek||06-26-2001||02:57 PM||||Well, there were some things bugging me about the faces I made, so I redid them. I especally didnt like the jpg fuzz that shows up. (I cam be a perfectionist sometimes) These pics are just scaled down jpgs, but if you want to actually use the images click on the links to give full bmps. Once again thanks to Ausfiero for getting me started on this.  One thing I would like to know is how he got the little hash marks so perfect...   anyways...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/gauges/speedosmall.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/gauges/tempandgassmall.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/gauges/tachsmall.jpg"> <P><BR>And if you want to see reg. size better quality use these:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/gauges/speedo.bmp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.oswg.net/Ted/gauges/speedo.bmp</A>  <A HREF="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/gauges/tempandgas.bmp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.oswg.net/Ted/gauges/tempandgas.bmp</A>  <A HREF="http://www.oswg.net/Ted/gauges/tach.bmp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.oswg.net/Ted/gauges/tach.bmp</A> ||||reg||1
