Z||000016||fierofrek||06-29-2001||01:02 PM||||yep, I took a pic of the original gauge, then "super" imposed it over a blank work area, then made the MPH marks, and then made the back round whatever color i wanted. Then i just print them out, and glued it to the gauges in the car. I used photo paper to give it a glossy look ( I have backlit gauges) and glued tin foil on the back of everything. I now have to "dim" the dash lights too bright.<P>as for "blacklight", it looks awsome, I have blacklights set up along the back window, and they make the gauges a perfect blue, and not to bright, but not to dim.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dsc_041.jpg">   <BR>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://members.tripod.com/fierofrek" TARGET=_blank>http://members.tripod.com/fierofrek</A> <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig3.jpg">    <P>PS, I forgot to put the temp needle back on. DOH!! I know already! LOL<p>[This message has been edited by fierofrek (edited 06-29-2001).]||||reg||1
